<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1814" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">algesco</span></b> , alsi, 3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch. n.</i>
			[algeo]. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To catch cold</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne ille alserit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Ad. 1, 1, 11</span></i>
			 (cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frigus colligere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 11, 13</span></i>
			, and perfrigescere, <i><span class="en">Juv. 7,
			194</span></i>).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Post-Aug. (cf. algens) of things, <i>to become
			cold</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(vites) aegrotant et, cum alsere, laesis
					uredine attonsarum oculis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					17, 24, 37, § 226</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rabies flammarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Apoth. 142</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
